Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 20:40:01 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1122/1178] The page in Russian, whole (1166, part one): every
 text the code makes, its pieces translated

The code's toasts, dialogs, menus, hints and tips were English in a Russian page: 1,307 new Russian keys
(heresy-i18n-ru.js, a block of its own after the old catalog), found by a scan of the code (toasts, dialogs, menu
labels, texts and tips set by code, the words inside HTML strings) and by harvesting the real page in Russian
(every room, menu, sheet, dialog, overlay and pane); the harvest went from 1,107 untranslated texts to 175, the rest
being names, formats, units and the cheat-sheet's own notes.

What the code glued from words, names and numbers is made translatable: tr() pieces where it is made (the run's line,
its seeds and stages, the take's eyebrow, the engine's detail, the output and slider and memory hints, the style meter,
the Writer's brief, the lyrics check's and the timing's summaries, the Trainer's says, gate and Train dialog, the GPU
hint), or spans of their own (the Librarian's summary, the cheat-sheet's counts, the Trainer's cards, picks and facts,
the Writer's list); drawn again when the language changes. Names stay as typed (translate="no"): take titles in the
take view and the player, the take ID, the workspaces in a take's menu (HeresyMenu raw items) and in the delete
dialog's select, the about list's places, the datasheet's head and its sliders' and LoRAs' names, model files, run
notes. The core sorts its patterns by their fixed text, so a longer pattern wins over a shorter one. Two homonyms
parted in English: the inspection's "pitch" (was "note"), the Train dialog's "Start training".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
